# Release signing for LocalDrop -- TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (same directory, drop the .example)
# and fill in the values you chose when creating the keystore. The real file is
# gitignored; this template is committed so a fresh clone knows what to create.
#
#     cp src-tauri/keystore.properties.example src-tauri/keystore.properties
#
# Both this file and the .jks must live in `src-tauri/`, NOT in the repo root
# and NOT under `src-tauri/gen/`. The Gradle signing config resolves them with
# `rootProject.file("../../")`, where rootProject is `src-tauri/gen/android` --
# so two levels up is `src-tauri/`. A copy anywhere else is not found, the
# properties stay empty, `storeFile` is null, the signing config is never
# applied, and Gradle emits `app-universal-release-unsigned.apk` after a full
# four-ABI LTO build with no error anywhere. The device then refuses to install
# it, saying only "App not installed".
#
# Create the keystore first, from the repo root:
#
#     keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore src-tauri/localdrop-release.jks \
#       -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000 -alias localdrop
#
# Then verify the config resolves, in seconds, without a build:
#
#     cd src-tauri/gen/android
#     powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass \
#       -File ../../../scripts/msvc-env.ps1 ./gradlew.bat -q :app:signingReport --console=plain
#
# The release variants must show your keystore, not the debug one.
#
# Keep the .jks and these passwords backed up somewhere outside the repo.
# Losing them means you cannot ship an update that upgrades an installed copy:
# Android treats a differently-signed APK as a different app and refuses to
# install over the old one. Anyone who obtains them can publish an update that
# Android accepts as genuine.
#
# See docs/BUILDING.md -> Signing.

# Path to the keystore, resolved relative to this file.
storeFile=localdrop-release.jks

# The -storepass you gave keytool.
storePassword=CHANGE_ME

# The -alias you gave keytool.
keyAlias=localdrop

# The -keypass you gave keytool. keytool defaults this to the store password
# when you accept the prompt with Enter, in which case repeat it here.
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
